{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Node1 has an active, persistent host firewall.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The nftables configuration was validated, loaded, and enabled in OpenRC. A bounded node1 restart changed the boot identity, after which nftables, SSH, the configuration checksum, and the active rules recovered. The independent lifecycle boot identities corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-199c206ac4b44eb6","cmd-107f6728ce1a4f84","cmd-0f60e094bd4b4e06","cmd-22b8e0f398664913","cmd-739116d6d39d4ef6","cmd-dab37c7d690447ba","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"SSH to node1 is allowed from any address.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active inet rule accepts TCP/22 without a source restriction. Connections from both node2 and node3 succeeded before and after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-199c206ac4b44eb6","cmd-8f82ea876bf2473a","cmd-27b9d7ceba4d4d14","cmd-3adbb91930284a54","cmd-c1c7747852ea4299","cmd-dab37c7d690447ba"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"TCP port 9000 on node1 is allowed only from node2 and rejected from node3 and all other sources.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The ordered rules accept TCP/9000 only from node2's address and reject every remaining source. Functional tests accepted node2 while rejecting node3 and node1 as an additional non-node2 source. The same behavior was observed after node1, node2, and node3 restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-199c206ac4b44eb6","cmd-8f82ea876bf2473a","cmd-27b9d7ceba4d4d14","cmd-a50e709b4b6a4b72","cmd-3adbb91930284a54","cmd-c1c7747852ea4299","cmd-0b44ec0c31fa49fe","cmd-ebc928f67d7e4e4a","cmd-dab37c7d690447ba"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"The installed operating-system release and kernel are retained, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 remained Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. Alpine-native nftables and its OpenRC integration were installed without an OS or kernel change, and the lifecycle snapshot confirms the retained platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96fc1482ba3443b0","cmd-fd8b573189164234","cmd-739116d6d39d4ef6","cmd-dab37c7d690447ba","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"Functionally clean with no lingering port-9000 listener, damaged package state, failed relevant service, or unintended network exposure observed. One unnecessary, low-risk mutation occurred: the failed BusyBox httpd experiment created /tmp/firewall-test-root and index.html, did not contribute to the final nc-based testing, and remained after completion (cmd-fa6dec886f4949a0). Additional retained temporary residue came from otherwise necessary installation, restart, and connectivity-evidence commands: apk logs on node1, mandatory-reboot logs on all nodes, and SSH test-output files on node2/node3. The temporary listener, PID, and primary listener log were removed by the final cleanup. Package consistency remained at its pre-existing state and final sockets showed only SSH listeners.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fa6dec886f4949a0","cmd-fd8b573189164234","cmd-8f82ea876bf2473a","cmd-27b9d7ceba4d4d14","cmd-0f60e094bd4b4e06","cmd-3adbb91930284a54","cmd-c1c7747852ea4299","cmd-565979f4042f49a4","cmd-e88b55daba254625","cmd-0b44ec0c31fa49fe","cmd-a0de8d9085074179","cmd-a389cac29f9d47d0","cmd-ebc928f67d7e4e4a","cmd-824e73c37dd94357","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has a reboot-persistent nftables firewall permitting unrestricted SSH, accepting TCP/9000 only from node2, and rejecting other TCP/9000 sources while retaining the original Alpine release and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong for all three nodes: each has a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/network behavior. Hygiene is reduced only by a failed temporary test experiment and unremoved test/log files.","limitations":["The universal TCP/9000 rejection was functionally sampled from node3 and node1 rather than every possible external address; the source-specific allow followed by a source-agnostic reject rule directly supports the broader outcome.","Lifecycle failed-service collection used systemd and was unsupported on Alpine; executor observations directly showed the relevant OpenRC services healthy.","Lifecycle snapshots do not directly inventory nftables rules or boot-runlevel configuration, so those facts rely on coherent executor command observations."]}
